Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.29,0:00:07.11,Cap,,0,0,0,,At 01:23 on 26 April 1986,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.56,0:00:10.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,Reactor Four of the Chernobyl\Nnuclear plant exploded.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.27,0:00:14.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,It caused the largest\Nuncontrolled release
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.40,0:00:17.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,of radioactivity ever recorded\Nfrom a civilian nuclear plant.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.17,0:00:22.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,This is what the record shows,\Nand what is still argued.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.63,0:00:30.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,Chernobyl lies in the north of Ukraine,\Nthen part of the Soviet Union,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.84,0:00:33.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,about one hundred ten\Nkilometres north of Kyiv.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.99,0:00:39.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,The power complex had four reactors\Nof a Soviet design called the RBMK,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.86,0:00:41.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,and two more were\Nunder construction.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.93,0:00:44.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,Beside it, a reservoir
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.50,0:00:47.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,of twenty two square kilometres\Nhad been built to cool the reactors.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.25,0:00:51.45,Cap,,0,0,0,,Three kilometres away stood Pripyat,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.80,0:00:54.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,a new city built for the plant's\Nworkers and their families.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.89,0:00:58.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,About forty nine thousand\Npeople lived there.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.45,0:01:04.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,The RBMK used graphite and boiling\Nwater, and it carried a serious flaw.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.07,0:01:09.43,Cap,,0,0,0,,At low power, more steam made\Nthe chain reaction stronger,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.50,0:01:11.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,and the reactor could\Nrun out of control.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.53,0:01:15.53,Cap,,0,0,0,,A Soviet state committee found in 1991
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.64,0:01:19.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,that the plant's operators had not\Nbeen made aware of this danger.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.29,0:01:25.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,On 25 April, the reactor was due to\Nshut down for routine maintenance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.53,0:01:29.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,Before it did, the crew planned a test
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.18,0:01:31.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,of whether a slowing\Nturbine could still
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.30,0:01:33.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,power the cooling pumps\Nduring a blackout.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.99,0:01:37.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,The same test had been tried the\Nyear before, and had not worked.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.19,0:01:44.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,At 14:00 on 25 April,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.92,0:01:48.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,the emergency cooling system\Nwas switched off for the test.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.69,0:01:50.33,Cap,,0,0,0,,The same hour,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.35,0:01:53.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,the Kyiv grid controller asked\Nfor the test to be postponed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.99,0:01:57.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,The reactor kept running at\Nreduced power into the night.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.09,0:02:03.23,Cap,,0,0,0,,At 00:28, as the power\Ncontrol was changed over,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.58,0:02:05.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,the power fell to almost nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.83,0:02:08.43,Cap,,0,0,0,,That was not in the test plan,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.50,0:02:11.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,and it left the reactor in an\Nextremely unstable condition.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.11,0:02:14.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,To raise the power again,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.80,0:02:17.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,the crew withdrew too\Nmany of the control rods.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.79,0:02:22.49,Cap,,0,0,0,,By 01:03 the power was only\Ntwo hundred megawatts,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.06,0:02:25.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,far below the planned level,\Nand the test went ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.21,0:02:30.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,Some of the automatic shutdown\Nsystems had been disabled.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.35,0:02:34.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,At 01:23, the test began.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.71,0:02:37.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,Thirty six seconds later,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.32,0:02:39.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,an operator pressed the\Nemergency shutdown button.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.23,0:02:42.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,A peculiarity in the design
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.80,0:02:45.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,of the control rods made the\Npower surge as they went in.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.49,0:02:51.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,In three seconds, the power passed\Nfive hundred thirty megawatts,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.54,0:02:54.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,more than twice the level at\Nwhich the test had begun.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.79,0:03:00.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,There was a steam explosion, and two\Nor three seconds later, a second one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.47,0:03:03.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,The reactor was destroyed,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.04,0:03:06.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,and burning graphite and fragments\Nof fuel were thrown out across the site.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.23,0:03:11.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,Two workers died in the\Nexplosions that night.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.51,0:03:18.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,Firefighters fought the fires on\Nthe roof of the turbine building,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.12,0:03:21.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,and put them out within a few hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.45,0:03:26.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,Within weeks, six of those firemen\Nwere among the people who had died
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.30,0:03:28.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,of acute radiation sickness.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.51,0:03:33.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,The fire in the reactor core\Nburned for about ten days.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.35,0:03:36.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,Water was pumped into\Nthe reactor for half a day,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.98,0:03:39.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,then stopped, for fear of\Nflooding the other units.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.07,0:03:42.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,From the second day,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.11,0:03:45.49,Cap,,0,0,0,,helicopters dropped about\Nfive thousand tonnes of boron,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.60,0:03:49.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,dolomite, sand, clay\Nand lead onto the core.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.21,0:03:52.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,One after another they carried them\Nout of here,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.91,0:03:57.26,Cap,,0,0,0,,such sacks of boron, dolomite, lead,\Nsand, clay.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.47,0:04:02.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,On 27 April, the city of\NPripyat was evacuated.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.83,0:04:05.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,A loudspeaker\Nannouncement told residents
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.90,0:04:08.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,that buses would arrive\Nfrom two in the afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.54,0:04:11.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,...a need arises
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.24,0:04:15.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,to carry out a temporary evacuation
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.39,0:04:16.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,of the city's residents.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.00,0:04:21.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,They were told to take documents,\Nessential things and food.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.84,0:04:26.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,About forty five thousand people\Nleft, and Pripyat was never resettled.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.86,0:04:31.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,By 14 May, about one hundred\Nsixteen thousand people
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.73,0:04:34.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,from within thirty kilometres of\Nthe plant had been evacuated.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.24,0:04:39.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,The wind carried radioactive\Ndust over Ukraine,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.17,0:04:42.27,Cap,,0,0,0,,Belarus and Russia,\Nand on across Europe.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.54,0:04:44.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,By 28 April,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.96,0:04:46.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,monitoring stations in Poland
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.79,0:04:50.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,and across Scandinavia were\Nrecording a radioactive cloud.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.38,0:04:55.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,On Italian television, the news anchor\Nreported what Moscow had said.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.34,0:04:58.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,Moscow's authorities confirm
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.68,0:05:00.83,Cap,,0,0,0,,that, contrary to what has been said\Nin many quarters,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.93,0:05:03.23,Cap,,0,0,0,,the accident has caused only two\Ndeaths.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.37,0:05:06.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,Several countries called the lack
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.08,0:05:09.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,of information from the Soviet\Nauthorities irresponsible.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.65,0:05:12.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,About two hundred\Nthousand liquidators,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.92,0:05:14.81,Cap,,0,0,0,,from all over the Soviet Union,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.04,0:05:18.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,took part in the clean-up\Nin 1986 and 1987.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.25,0:05:23.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,Some cleared radioactive\Ndebris from the roofs by hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.55,0:05:26.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,In a Soviet film of the time,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.48,0:05:28.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,physicists measured\Nthe dose at each spot
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.06,0:05:31.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,and set the time limit for each worker.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.13,0:05:34.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,Before these figures became known and\Nunderstood,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.38,0:05:37.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,the roentgens, the minutes,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.18,0:05:39.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,physicists had to go through\Neverywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.32,0:05:43.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,Armoured machines and remote\Ncontrolled equipment were sent
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.33,0:05:44.89,Cap,,0,0,0,,to the most dangerous places.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.21,0:05:49.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,These specialised machines went in,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.66,0:05:53.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,with armoured cabs lined with lead.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.56,0:05:56.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,The same film said that\Nthe danger remained
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.73,0:05:59.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,that the core might melt\Ndown into the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.20,0:06:04.39,Cap,,0,0,0,,Within seven months,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.83,0:06:08.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,a concrete shelter was built\Naround the ruined reactor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.36,0:06:13.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,It was built in haste, and designed\Nto last only twenty to thirty years.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.74,0:06:19.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,In 2016, a steel arch one hundred ten\Nmetres high was slid over it on rails.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.26,0:06:25.81,Cap,,0,0,0,,The last working reactor at Chernobyl\Nwas shut down in December 2000.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.28,0:06:29.51,Cap,,0,0,0,,Workers and their families\Nmoved to a new town,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.53,0:06:32.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,Slavutich, thirty\Nkilometres from the plant.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.28,0:06:38.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,Officially, thirty plant workers and\Nfiremen died within three months.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.62,0:06:40.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,After that,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.70,0:06:44.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,United Nations scientists linked\Nabout five thousand thyroid cancers
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.69,0:06:45.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,to the accident,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.87,0:06:48.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,and fifteen of those\Nwere fatal by 2005.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.80,0:06:53.45,Cap,,0,0,0,,They found no clear evidence\Nof a major rise in other cancers.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.80,0:06:57.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,Estimates of the eventual\Ndeath toll still differ widely:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.87,0:07:00.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,a United Nations report\Npredicted about four thousand,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.71,0:07:04.53,Cap,,0,0,0,,and in 2006 Greenpeace estimated\Nmore than ninety thousand.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.18,0:07:09.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,The first official account, in\N1986, blamed the operators.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.18,0:07:14.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,In 1992, an international\Ngroup put more weight
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.51,0:07:15.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,on the design of the reactor.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.40,0:07:22.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,Valery Legasov, who led the Soviet\Ndelegation to the IAEA review,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.09,0:07:25.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,wrote that it was impossible\Nto find a single culprit.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.92,0:07:30.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,Caesium one thirty seven, one\Nof the main contaminants,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.43,0:07:32.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,has a half life of thirty years.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.88,0:07:37.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,About a thousand people returned to\Nlive in the zone without permission.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.62,0:07:41.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,In 2011, the zone was\Nopened to tourists,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.67,0:07:45.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,and visits peaked at about\None hundred thousand in 2019.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.54,0:07:51.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,In 2022, Russian forces took control\Nof the site for about five weeks.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.68,0:07:56.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,The Exclusion Zone began as\Na circle thirty kilometres wide,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.63,0:08:00.17,Cap,,0,0,0,,and now covers about four thousand\Nthree hundred square kilometres.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.68,0:08:03.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,The reactor was destroyed in seconds,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.93,0:08:06.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,but the argument over who was\Nto blame has lasted decades.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.50,0:08:11.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,If the flaw was known, who\Nshould have told the operators?
